# XQ Squad (Cursor adapter)

This repository uses XQ Squad. `.squad/` is the canonical source of truth; this rule only maps it onto Cursor.

- The main Cursor Agent is the **Agent Lead**. Follow `.squad/agents/lead.md` and the 8-stage workflow in `.squad/workflows/delivery.md`. Read `.squad/README.md` for layout.
- Use the `squad-delivery` skill for build/fix/change requests.
- Delegate to the `analyst`, `implementer`, `tester`, `reviewer`, and `memory-maintainer` subagents in `.cursor/agents/`. Give each one an explicit task and write scope. If a subagent isn't available, perform the role yourself from `.squad/agents/<role>.md`.
- Subagents share this checkout. Cursor's isolated subagent copies are **not** squad isolation. Separate concurrent deliveries must follow `.squad/workflows/concurrent-delivery.md`: one approved worktree under `.squad/worktrees/<delivery-id>` with a scope claim each. Overlapping scopes hard-block.
- Load only relevant memory (`node .squad/scripts/memory-search.mjs`). Memory and knowledge stay in `.squad/`, never in `.cursor/`.
- Verify before reporting success. Report memory status as `UPDATED`, `UNCHANGED`, or `BLOCKED`.
- Never commit, push, or open a PR/release unless the user explicitly authorizes it. The `xq-squad-git-guard` hook asks the user to confirm each one.
- The hooks in `.cursor/hooks.json` supplement these contracts. They do not replace them. A hook denial is a governance block: report it and don't work around it.
